WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
The production market catalog is open in a Privy-authenticated session. Layrs exposes aggregate odds while keeping the user’s balances, orders and positions private.

00:12.000 --> 00:24.000
The live ZEN market shows the public Pyth reference chart and the private order surface. Individual resting orders are processed inside the attested private CLOB.

00:24.000 --> 00:36.000
The Privacy page verifies the current TEE release in the browser. Funding uses controlled deposit sessions while the private ledger remains the portfolio source of truth.

00:36.000 --> 00:50.000
Portfolio values and LP ownership are user-scoped. The vault surface publishes aggregate assets and strategy state without publishing the user-to-position mapping.

00:50.000 --> 01:03.000
Resolved-market history preserves the public outcome and settlement evidence after private execution has finished.

01:03.000 --> 01:18.000
Iteration 0 uses RISC Zero to prove the deterministic 25-observation median resolution and settlement commitment. zkVerify verifies the receipt.

01:18.000 --> 01:30.000
Layrs publishes the proof hash and settlement commitment to the non-custodial registry on Horizen. The adoption report exposes reconciled aggregates, not private identity mappings.

01:30.000 --> 01:49.000
The public deployment registry links the RISC Zero image ID, zkVerify verification transaction, Horizen proof-registry contract and attestation transaction for independent review.

01:49.000 --> 02:09.200
The adoption surface reports only qualifying protocol activity. Test wallets, dust, duplicate identities and failed transactions are excluded from Guardian-qualified totals.
